IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`
IMPORT `sga-part2`

-- sga-part3a.l4: Part 3, Division 1 (sections 15B and 15C) and Division 2, Subdivisions A to C as far as section 18B
-- (sections 16A, 17A to 17D, 18A, 18B) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- The simplified outlines (sections 16, 17 and 18) are not rules and are not encoded; NOTES.md says so.
-- Where the text makes the Commissioner's satisfaction or opinion the condition, the satisfaction or opinion is a plain input.

§ `Division 1: former employees, and certificates of coverage`

-- src:375 | 15B Application of Part to former employees
-- src:376 | This Part applies to payments of qualifying earnings to or for a former employee as if the former employee were an employee of the person who was the former employee’s employer.
@ref s 15B (src:375-376)
GIVEN `the person was the employer of the former employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 3 treats the former employee as an employee of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was the employer of the former employee` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:378 | (1) This section applies if a scheduled international social security agreement (within the meaning of section 5 of the Social Security (International Agreements) Act 1999) prevents double coverage of the compulsory retirement savings arrangements under the laws of the parties to the agreement.
@ref s 15C(1) to (3) (src:378-378)
-- src:379 | (2) An entity mentioned in subsection (3) may apply in writing to the Commissioner for a certificate under subsection (4) covering the employment of a particular employee.
@ref s 15C(1) to (3) (src:379-379)
-- src:380 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the entity must be:
-- src:381 | (a) if the employee’s employer is not a resident of Australia—a related entity (within the meaning of the agreement) of the employer; or
-- src:382 | (b) otherwise—the employee’s employer.
@ref s 15C(1) to (3) (src:380-382)
GIVEN `a scheduled international social security agreement prevents double coverage of the compulsory retirement savings arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a resident of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is the employer of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a related entity of the employer within the meaning of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an entity may apply in writing for a certificate of coverage` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a scheduled international social security agreement prevents double coverage of the compulsory retirement savings arrangements`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the employer is a resident of Australia` THEN JUST `the entity is the employer of the employee`
           OTHERWISE JUST `the entity is a related entity of the employer within the meaning of the agreement`

-- src:383 | (4) The Commissioner may give the entity that made the application a certificate under this subsection if the Commissioner is satisfied that doing so is in accordance with the agreement mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 15C(4) (src:383-383)
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied that giving the certificate is in accordance with the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may give the entity that applied a certificate of coverage` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner is satisfied that giving the certificate is in accordance with the agreement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:384 | (5) The certificate must:
-- src:385 | (a) state the name of the employer and the employee; and
-- src:386 | (b) state the time at which, or the circumstances in which, the certificate stops covering the employment; and
-- src:387 | (c) contain any other information that the Commissioner considers relevant.
@ref s 15C(5) (src:384-387)
GIVEN `it states the name of the employer and the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the time at which, or the circumstances in which, the certificate stops covering the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains any other information that the Commissioner considers relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a certificate of coverage has the required content` MEANS
        `it states the name of the employer and the employee`
    AND `it states the time at which, or the circumstances in which, the certificate stops covering the employment`
    AND `it contains any other information that the Commissioner considers relevant`

-- src:388 | (6) The Commissioner may revoke or vary a certificate under subsection (4), if doing so would be in accordance with the administrative arrangements to the agreement mentioned in subsection (1) that are agreed between the parties to the agreement.
@ref s 15C(6) (src:388-388)
GIVEN `revoking or varying the certificate would be in accordance with the administrative arrangements agreed between the parties to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may revoke or vary a certificate of coverage` MEANS
    IF `revoking or varying the certificate would be in accordance with the administrative arrangements agreed between the parties to the agreement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:389 | (7) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (4) or (6) may object against the decision in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 15C(7) (src:389-389)
GIVEN `the person is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (4) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may object against the decision in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` MEANS
    IF `the person is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (4) or (6)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:390 | (8) If the entity that made the application is not the employee’s employer, this Part (apart from this section) applies to qualifying earnings relating to employment covered by the certificate that are paid to the employee as if the entity that made the application were the employee’s employer.
@ref s 15C(8) (src:390-390)
GIVEN `the entity that made the application is the employer of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying earnings relate to employment covered by the certificate and are paid to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Part treats the entity that made the application as the employer of the employee` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the entity that made the application is the employer of the employee`)) AND `the qualifying earnings relate to employment covered by the certificate and are paid to the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 16A: who pays the charge`

-- src:402 | 16A Superannuation guarantee charge payable by employers
-- src:403 | Superannuation guarantee charge imposed on an employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day is payable by the employer.
@ref s 16A (src:402-403)
GIVEN `the charge is imposed on the superannuation guarantee shortfall of the employer for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the charge on the shortfall of an employer for a QE day is payable by the employer` MEANS
    IF `the charge is imposed on the superannuation guarantee shortfall of the employer for the QE day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subdivision B: individual superannuation guarantee amounts (sections 17A to 17D)`

-- src:430 | charge percentage means 12.
@ref s 17A(2) "charge percentage" (src:430-430)
`the charge percentage` MEANS 12

-- 17A(2) "amount of the qualifying earnings": (a) one payment, its amount; (b) two or more, the sum. Each payment is first treated as section 10A(6) provides.
-- src:426 | amount of the qualifying earnings means:
-- src:427 | (a) if there is one such payment—the amount of the payment; or
-- src:428 | (b) if there are 2 or more such payments—the sum of the amounts of the payments.
-- src:429 | Note: If the payment of qualifying earnings is in the form of a reduction so that a sacrificed contribution can be made, the amount of the payment is the amount of the reduction (see paragraph 10A(1)(h)).
@ref s 17A(2) "amount of the qualifying earnings" (src:426-429)
GIVEN `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer earlier in the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the base for the year` IS A NUMBER
      payments IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the qualifying earnings on the QE day` MEANS
    CONSIDER payments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the sum of two amounts` (`the amount of the payment that is treated as qualifying earnings` `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer earlier in the financial year` p `the base for the year`) (`the amount of the qualifying earnings on the QE day` (`the sum of two amounts` `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer earlier in the financial year` p) `the base for the year` rest)

-- 17A(2): the amount of qualifying earnings x (charge percentage / 100). 17B: an exemption certificate in force for the employee and employer over a period that includes the QE day
-- treats the employee as having already reached the maximum contributions base, so the amount of the payment is nil.
-- src:422 | (1) This Subdivision applies if an employer makes a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee on a particular day (the QE day).
-- src:423 | Note: This includes reducing the employee’s earnings so that a sacrificed contribution can be made for the employee (see paragraphs 10A(1)(h) and (4)(b)).
@ref s 17A(1), (2), s 17B (src:422-423)
-- src:424 | (2) On the QE day, the employer has an individual superannuation guarantee amount for the employee equal to:
-- src:425 | where:
@ref s 17A(1), (2), s 17B (src:424-425)
-- src:431 | 17B An exemption certificate can reduce this amount to nil
-- src:432 | However, if an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for the employee in relation to:
-- src:433 | (a) the employer; and
-- src:434 | (b) a period that includes the QE day;
-- src:435 | treat the employee as having already reached the maximum contributions base before the QE day.
-- src:436 | Note 1: This means:
-- src:437 | (a) the amount of the payment of qualifying earnings on the QE day is treated as if it were nil (see subsection 10A(6)); and
-- src:438 | (b) the individual superannuation guarantee amount is nil.
-- src:439 | Note 2: If the employee has more than one employer and the certificate is issued in relation to only this employer, then the certificate does not affect the other employers’ individual superannuation guarantee amounts.
@ref s 17A(1), (2), s 17B (src:431-439)
GIVEN `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer earlier in the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the base for the year` IS A NUMBER
      payments IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for the employee in relation to the employer and a period that includes the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the individual superannuation guarantee amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER payments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (qe TIMES (`the charge percentage` DIVIDED BY 100))
    WHERE
        earlier MEANS IF `an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for the employee in relation to the employer and a period that includes the QE day` THEN `the base for the year` ELSE `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer earlier in the financial year`
        qe MEANS `the amount of the qualifying earnings on the QE day` earlier `the base for the year` payments

-- src:442 | (1) The Commissioner may, on application by an employee, issue a certificate (an employer shortfall exemption certificate) to the applicant for:
-- src:443 | (a) a specified employer of the applicant at the time the application is made; and
-- src:444 | (b) a specified period ending at the end of a specified financial year;
-- src:445 | if the Commissioner is satisfied of the matters in subsection (2).
@ref s 17C(1) to (3) (src:442-445)
-- src:446 | (2) The matters are that:
-- src:447 | (a) if the certificate is not issued, the applicant is likely to have excess concessional contributions for that financial year (whether or not issuing the certificate would prevent that result); and
-- src:448 | (b) if the certificate is issued for that period, at least one other employer of the applicant is likely to have an individual superannuation guarantee amount for:
-- src:449 | (i) the applicant; and
-- src:450 | (ii) a QE day during that financial year;
-- src:451 | that is greater than nil; and
-- src:452 | (c) it is appropriate in the circumstances to issue the certificate.
@ref s 17C(1) to (3) (src:446-452)
-- src:453 | (3) When considering a matter in subsection (2), the Commissioner:
-- src:454 | (a) for the matter in paragraph (2)(a) or (b)—must have regard to any other employer shortfall exemption certificate that has been issued, or is proposed to be issued, to the applicant for that financial year; and
-- src:455 | (b) for the matter in paragraph (2)(c)—may have regard to:
-- src:456 | (i) the effect that issuing the certificate is likely to have on the applicant’s concessional contributions for that financial year; and
-- src:457 | (ii) any other matter that the Commissioner considers relevant.
-- src:458 | Application for certificate
@ref s 17C(1) to (3) (src:453-458)
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied that the applicant is likely to have excess concessional contributions for the financial year if the certificate is not issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied that at least one other employer of the applicant is likely to have an individual superannuation guarantee amount greater than nil for the applicant and a QE day in the financial year if the certificate is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied that it is appropriate in the circumstances to issue the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may issue an employer shortfall exemption certificate` MEANS
    IF     `the Commissioner is satisfied that the applicant is likely to have excess concessional contributions for the financial year if the certificate is not issued`
       AND `the Commissioner is satisfied that at least one other employer of the applicant is likely to have an individual superannuation guarantee amount greater than nil for the applicant and a QE day in the financial year if the certificate is issued`
       AND `the Commissioner is satisfied that it is appropriate in the circumstances to issue the certificate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:459 | (4) An application for an employer shortfall exemption certificate:
-- src:460 | (a) must be in the approved form; and
-- src:461 | (b) must specify the employer, period and financial year to be specified in the certificate; and
-- src:462 | (c) must be made at least 30 days before the first day of the period.
-- src:463 | Objections and other matters
@ref s 17C(4) (src:459-463)
GIVEN `the application is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application specifies the employer, the period and the financial year to be specified in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an application for an employer shortfall exemption certificate meets section 17C(4)` MEANS
        `the application is in the approved form`
    AND `the application specifies the employer, the period and the financial year to be specified in the certificate`
    AND `an application is made at least 30 days before the first day of the period` `the day the application is made` `the first day of the period`

-- src:464 | (5) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (1) may object against the decision in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 17C(5) (src:464-464)
GIVEN `the person is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may object against the decision under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` MEANS
    IF `the person is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commissioner under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:465 | (6) The Commissioner may not vary or revoke an employer shortfall exemption certificate.
@ref s 17C(6) (src:465-465)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may vary or revoke an employer shortfall exemption certificate` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:466 | (7) An employer shortfall exemption certificate:
-- src:467 | (a) may be issued after the first day of the period specified in the certificate; and
-- src:468 | (b) is not a legislative instrument.
@ref s 17C(7) (src:466-468)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an employer shortfall exemption certificate may be issued after the first day of the period specified in it` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:466 | (7) An employer shortfall exemption certificate:
-- src:467 | (a) may be issued after the first day of the period specified in the certificate; and
-- src:468 | (b) is not a legislative instrument.
@ref s 17C(7) (src:466-468)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an employer shortfall exemption certificate is a legislative instrument` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:470 | (1) If the Commissioner makes a decision under subsection 17C(1) about an application, the Commissioner must give written notice of the decision to:
-- src:471 | (a) the applicant; and
-- src:472 | (b) if the decision is to issue a certificate—the employer to which the certificate relates.
@ref s 17D(1), (2) (src:470-472)
-- src:473 | (2) A notice of a decision to issue a certificate must include a copy of the certificate.
@ref s 17D(1), (2) (src:473-473)
GIVEN `the decision is to issue a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the people the Commissioner must give written notice of a decision under subsection 17C(1) to` MEANS
    IF `the decision is to issue a certificate`
    THEN LIST "the applicant", "the employer to which the certificate relates"
    ELSE LIST "the applicant"

-- src:473 | (2) A notice of a decision to issue a certificate must include a copy of the certificate.
@ref s 17D(2) (src:473-473)
GIVEN `the notice includes a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a notice of a decision to issue a certificate meets section 17D(2)` MEANS `the notice includes a copy of the certificate`

§ `Subdivision C: eligible contributions (sections 18A and 18B)`

DECLARE `Contribution made for the benefit of an employee` HAS
    `is a sacrificed contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to a complying superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made at a time when a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to an RSA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is able to be allocated within the RSA for the benefit of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee has died, and the employer instead pays an equivalent of a contribution that it would otherwise have made under paragraph (a) or (b) to the legal personal representative of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is notionally made as described in subsection (3) to a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before or at the time it is made the employer has obtained a written statement by or for the trustee that the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 18B(2) applies on the day the contribution is made` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 18A(2): conclusively presumed to be to a complying superannuation fund if the written statement was obtained; 18B(1)(a): the presumption is unavailable if 18B(2) applies on the day.
-- src:502 | (2) A contribution made by the employer for the benefit of the employee to a superannuation fund is conclusively presumed to be a contribution to a complying superannuation fund for the purposes of subparagraph (1)(a)(i) if:
-- src:503 | (a) at or before the time the contribution is made, the employer has obtained a written statement provided by or on behalf of the trustee of the fund; and
-- src:504 | (b) the statement provides that the fund:
-- src:505 | (i) is a resident regulated superannuation fund; and
-- src:506 | (ii) is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993.
-- src:507 | Note 1: The presumption does not extend to any of the other elements of paragraph (1)(a), such as that the contribution must not be a sacrificed contribution.
-- src:508 | Note 2: The presumption may not always be available (see section 18B).
-- src:509 | Notional contributions for defined benefit members of defined benefit superannuation schemes
@ref s 18A(2), s 18B(1)(a) (src:502-509)
-- src:527 | (1) However:
@ref s 18A(2), s 18B(1)(a) (src:527-527)
-- src:528 | (a) the presumption in subsection 18A(2) is unavailable for a contribution to a fund if subsection (2) of this section applies on the day the contribution is made; or
@ref s 18A(2), s 18B(1)(a) (src:528-528)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution made for the benefit of an employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the contribution is treated as to a complying superannuation fund` MEANS
        c's `is to a complying superannuation fund`
    OR (    c's `before or at the time it is made the employer has obtained a written statement by or for the trustee that the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993`
        AND NOT (c's `section 18B(2) applies on the day the contribution is made`))

-- 18A(1): the meaning of eligible contribution, limbs (a) to (d). The text introduces the list with "is:" and no limb adds a closing word; it is taken as the definition (a defined term, section 6(1)).
-- src:485 | (1) An eligible contribution, made by an employer for the benefit of an employee, is:
-- src:486 | (a) a contribution (other than a sacrificed contribution) made by the employer for the benefit of the employee that:
-- src:487 | (i) is to a complying superannuation fund; and
-- src:488 | (ii) is able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee; and
-- src:489 | (iii) is not made for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme; and
-- src:490 | (iv) is not made at a time when a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund; or
-- src:491 | (b) a contribution (other than a sacrificed contribution) made by the employer for the benefit of the employee:
-- src:492 | (i) to an RSA; and
-- src:493 | (ii) that is able to be allocated within the RSA for the benefit of the employee; or
-- src:494 | (c) if:
-- src:495 | (i) the employee has died; and
-- src:496 | (ii) the employer would, if the employee had not died, have made a contribution covered by paragraph (a) or (b) for the benefit of the employee; and
-- src:497 | (iii) the employer instead pays an equivalent amount to the employee’s legal personal representative;
-- src:498 | that equivalent amount paid by the employer; or
-- src:499 | (d) a contribution notionally made as described in subsection (3) to a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of the scheme.
-- src:500 | Note: For the purposes of subparagraphs (a)(ii) and (b)(ii), regulations under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 and under the Retirement Savings Accounts Act 1997 deal with the allocation of contributions.
-- src:501 | Presumption for contributions to certain superannuation funds
@ref s 18A(1) (src:485-501)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution made for the benefit of an employee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an eligible contribution` MEANS
    JUST (`limb a` OR `limb b` OR `limb c` OR `limb d`)
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS (NOT (c's `is a sacrificed contribution`)) AND `the contribution is treated as to a complying superannuation fund` c AND c's `is able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee` AND (NOT (c's `is made for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme`)) AND (NOT (c's `is made at a time when a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund`))
        `limb b` MEANS (NOT (c's `is a sacrificed contribution`)) AND c's `is to an RSA` AND c's `is able to be allocated within the RSA for the benefit of the employee`
        `limb c` MEANS c's `the employee has died, and the employer instead pays an equivalent of a contribution that it would otherwise have made under paragraph (a) or (b) to the legal personal representative of the employee`
        `limb d` MEANS c's `is notionally made as described in subsection (3) to a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member of the scheme`

-- 18B(2): the employer is, or is associated with, the trustee or manager, and reasonably believes the fund is not a resident regulated superannuation fund or is operating in contravention of a regulatory provision.
-- src:530 | (2) This subsection applies on a day if, on that day:
-- src:531 | (a) one of the following subparagraphs applies:
-- src:532 | (i) the employer is the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme;
-- src:533 | (ii) the employer is an associate of the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme;
-- src:534 | (iii) the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme is an associate of the employer; and
-- src:535 | (b) the employer reasonably believes that the fund or scheme:
-- src:536 | (i) is not a resident regulated superannuation fund; or
-- src:537 | (ii) is operating in contravention of a regulatory provision (within the meaning of section 38A of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993).
@ref s 18B(2), (3) (src:530-537)
-- src:538 | (3) Section 39 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 applies for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) of this section in a corresponding way to the way that section applies for the purposes of Division 2 of Part 5 of that Act.
-- src:539 | Note: Section 39 of that Act allows certain contraventions to be ignored.
@ref s 18B(2), (3) (src:538-539)
GIVEN `the employer is the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is an associate of the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme is an associate of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer reasonably believes that the fund or scheme is not a resident regulated superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer reasonably believes that the fund or scheme is operating in contravention of a regulatory provision, and the contravention is not one that section 39 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 allows to be ignored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 18B(2) applies on the day` MEANS
        (`the employer is the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme` OR `the employer is an associate of the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme` OR `the trustee or manager of the fund or scheme is an associate of the employer`)
    AND (`the employer reasonably believes that the fund or scheme is not a resident regulated superannuation fund` OR `the employer reasonably believes that the fund or scheme is operating in contravention of a regulatory provision, and the contravention is not one that section 39 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 allows to be ignored`)

-- 18A(3): the notional contribution for a defined benefit member: the amount of the qualifying earnings x the notional employer contribution rate (a percentage, section 10(1)).
-- src:510 | (3) If, on a QE day for the employer and the employee:
-- src:511 | (a) a benefit certificate for a defined benefit superannuation scheme has effect; and
-- src:512 | (b) the scheme is operating for the benefit of the employee:
-- src:513 | (i) as a defined benefit member of the scheme; and
-- src:514 | (ii) in relation to payments of qualifying earnings to or for the employee by the employer; and
-- src:515 | (c) the benefit certificate:
-- src:516 | (i) covers a class of employees (that includes the employee) as defined benefit members of the scheme; and
-- src:517 | (ii) specifies the notional employer contribution rate in relation to that class of employees; and
-- src:518 | (d) the employer has a written statement, provided by or on behalf of the trustee of the scheme, that the scheme:
-- src:519 | (i) is a resident regulated superannuation fund; and
-- src:520 | (ii) is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993; and
-- src:521 | (iii) has not been subject to such a direction at any time since the beginning of the day on which the benefit certificate is expressed to take effect;
-- src:522 | treat the scheme as having received, on the QE day, a notional contribution made by the employer for the benefit of the employee that is equal to:
-- src:523 | where:
-- src:524 | amount of the qualifying earnings has the same meaning as in subsection 17A(2) for the one or more payments of qualifying earnings to or for the employee made by the employer on the QE day.
-- src:525 | Note: The written statement may not always have effect (see section 18B).
@ref s 18A(3), s 18B(1)(b) (src:510-525)
-- src:527 | (1) However:
@ref s 18A(3), s 18B(1)(b) (src:527-527)
-- src:529 | (b) a statement provided as described in paragraph 18A(3)(d) has no effect for a scheme if subsection (2) of this section applies on the QE day.
@ref s 18A(3), s 18B(1)(b) (src:529-529)
GIVEN `a benefit certificate for the scheme has effect on the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is operating for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member in relation to payments of qualifying earnings by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit certificate covers a class of employees that includes the employee and specifies the notional employer contribution rate for that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has a written statement by or for the trustee that the scheme is a resident regulated superannuation fund, is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 and has not been subject to such a direction since the benefit certificate was expressed to take effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 18B(2) applies on the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the qualifying earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the notional employer contribution rate, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the notional contribution for a defined benefit member` MEANS
    IF     `a benefit certificate for the scheme has effect on the QE day`
       AND `the scheme is operating for the benefit of the employee as a defined benefit member in relation to payments of qualifying earnings by the employer`
       AND `the benefit certificate covers a class of employees that includes the employee and specifies the notional employer contribution rate for that class`
       AND `the employer has a written statement by or for the trustee that the scheme is a resident regulated superannuation fund, is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 and has not been subject to such a direction since the benefit certificate was expressed to take effect`
       AND (NOT (`subsection 18B(2) applies on the QE day`))
    THEN JUST (`the amount of the qualifying earnings` TIMES (`the notional employer contribution rate, as a percentage` DIVIDED BY 100))
    ELSE NOTHING
